The allocation tests of numeric ancestry classification no longer fail intermittently (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/394). `GC.GetAllocatedBytesForCurrentThread` also counts what the runtime allocates on the measuring thread while it recompiles warm code, so a single measured loop could be charged for a one-off runtime allocation. Each test now runs its measured loop once unmeasured, then measures identical loops, up to ten, until one allocates nothing; an allocation made by the classification itself recurs in every loop and still fails the test. Two new tests check the measurement itself: an allocation on every run is charged, and an allocation in one loop only is not. A failure now reports each loop's allocated bytes and the methods compiled on the measuring thread. Test-only; no product change.
